==Latvian==
{{slim-wikipedia|lang=lv}}
[[File:Jökulsárlón17.jpg|thumb|250px|Ledus]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|bat-pro|lv}} {{recons|led-|lang=bat-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|lv}} {{recons|ledʰ||ice|lang=ine-pro}}, perhaps the same as {{recons|leidʰ||slippery, to slide|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognates include {{etyl|lt|-}} {{term|ledas|lẽdas|lang=lt}}, dialectal {{term|ledus|ledùs|lang=lt}}, {{etyl|prg|-}} {{term|ladis|lang=prg}}, {{etyl|ru|-}} {{term|лёд|tr=ljod|lang=ru}}, {{etyl|cu|-}} {{term|лєдъ|tr=ledŭ|lang=cu}}, {{etyl|cs|-}} {{term|led|lang=cs}}, {{etyl|pl|-}} {{term|lód|lang=pl}}.<ref>{{R:lv:LEV}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{lv-IPA|lædus}}
{{rfap|lang=lv}}

===Noun===
{{lv-noun|m|3rd}}

# [[ice]], [[frozen]] [[water]]
#: '''''ledus''' kristāli'' — '''ice''' cristals
#: '''''ledus''' slānis'' — '''ice''' layer
#: ''plāns '''ledus''' — thin '''ice'''
#: ''lauzt '''ledu''''' — to break the ice  
#: '''''ledus''' kūst, lūst, krakšķ'' — the '''ice''' melts, breaks, cracks
#: ''auksts kā '''ledus''''' — cold as '''ice'''
#: '''''ledus''' skapis, '''ledus'''skapis — '''ice''' cupboard (= refrigerator) 
#: '''''ledus''' balets'' — ballet (skating) on '''ice'''

